Give ares_resolver.cc the ns_* enums on OpenBSD.

c-ares defines ns_c_in, ns_t_srv, ... only without a system <arpa/nameser.h>,
and OpenBSD's has none of them ("use of undeclared identifier 'ns_c_in'").
grpc's event_engine/nameser.h defines them where GRPC_HAVE_ARPA_NAMESER is
unset, which includes OpenBSD.  Guarded so Windows (no <arpa/nameser.h>, so
c-ares defines them itself) does not see a second definition.

--- a/src/core/lib/event_engine/ares_resolver.cc
+++ b/src/core/lib/event_engine/ares_resolver.cc
@@ -38,6 +38,12 @@
 #if ARES_VERSION >= 0x011200
 // c-ares 1.18.0 or later starts to provide ares_nameser.h as a public header.
 #include <ares_nameser.h>
+#if defined(GPR_OPENBSD)
+// cvcpkg: c-ares defines the BIND 8 ns_* enums only when the system has no
+// <arpa/nameser.h>, and OpenBSD's has none of them; grpc's own header defines
+// them where GRPC_HAVE_ARPA_NAMESER is unset, which includes OpenBSD.
+#include "src/core/lib/event_engine/nameser.h"  // IWYU pragma: keep
+#endif
 #else
 #include "src/core/lib/event_engine/nameser.h"  // IWYU pragma: keep
 #endif
